From: oveRTOS <noreply@invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] mps2-an500: link kernel RAM into SSRAM2&3, not the 16M block

The board has three RAM regions, and NuttX's flash.ld puts .data/.bss (and
therefore the heap, via CONFIG_RAM_START) at 0x60000000 — the 16 MB block QEMU
calls mps.ram. That is the only region large enough to stage the Linux
personality's rootfs.cpio, so kernel RAM and the rootfs contend for it: NuttX's
startup copies .data over the CPIO header and zeroes .bss across it, and the
parse fails.

SSRAM2&3 at 0x20000000 (4 MB, QEMU mps.ssram23) is real RAM and unused — it is
where the FreeRTOS port already keeps its data, which is why FreeRTOS leaves the
16 MB block free. Link kernel RAM there and hand 0x60000000 to the personality.

4 MB is ample: .data + .bss are ~200 KB, leaving ~3.8 MB of heap versus the
~1.8 MB the previous 2 MB CONFIG_RAM_SIZE allowed.

--- a/boards/arm/mps/mps2-an500/scripts/flash.ld
+++ b/boards/arm/mps/mps2-an500/scripts/flash.ld
@@ -23,7 +23,7 @@
 MEMORY
 {
   flash (rx)  : ORIGIN = 0x00000000, LENGTH = 4M
-  sram1 (rwx) : ORIGIN = 0x60000000, LENGTH = 16M
+  sram1 (rwx) : ORIGIN = 0x20000000, LENGTH = 4M
 }
 
 OUTPUT_ARCH(arm)
